tter to  break it up at this point so that you  get something accomplished  i  i don't want to negotiate against myself  here because of course we love all the  parts to it but we need to get something  accomplished yes and we need to get  everybody on absolutely the child tax  and universal child care we no we need  to get those accomplished we need to get  those through right but peel them off to  pass them individually so they can get  through that's right but remember we're  back to the filibuster problem but  you're open to breaking it up though  i'm open to whatever's going to get us  across the finish line knowing we're not  going to get one single republican to  lower the price of prescription drugs  not one to give us universal child care  not one who's going to say that these  corporations that make billions in  profits are going to not get away any  longer with paying zero in taxes we've  got all those in buildback better we  just need to get  what we can across the finish line in  2024 should mansion and cinema be  primary  we'll we'll address that when we get  past this week okay let me ask you about  2024 do you believe that president biden  is up for the job president biden's  running for reelection i expect to  support him the his approval ratings are  some of the lowest that they've been for  a very long time i i understand that but  remember we've just finished the first  quarter we're just starting into the  second quarter here so we've got a lot  of time a lot of work in front of us oh  but you only have probably less than a  year uh before you lose both the senate  and the house all the polls  are very very very bad right i mean the  gallup had a poll recently that showed a  preference nationally for republicans at  a five-point margin over democrats you  started the year with the insurrection  and a nine point advantage in the fourth  quarter it was a five-point advantage to  the republicans so something's not right  here something that you think it could  change the game for president biden is  with a stroke of a pen he could cancel  student loan debt federally yes why do  you think that would make such a  difference because it would affect about  43 million americans and keep in mind  for the people who are dealing with  student loan debt  about 40 percent of them do not have  college diplomas these are people who  did what we want them to do as americans  they tried but  they had babies they were working three  jobs they moved and they didn't make it  so now they're dealing with student loan  debt on what a high school grant makes  also think about the racial implications  of what we're talking about we talk  about the racial wealth gap in america  it's alive and well right in the heart  of the student loan debt problem african  americans borrow more money to go to  school borrow more money while they're  in school borrow have a harder time  paying when they get out  the single thing that president biden  could do all by himself to help close  the black white wealth gap for people  with student loan debt he could close it  by 27 points cancel 50 000 in student  loan debt same thing for latinos this  would be a huge difference but in so  many words he has said that this is  bigger than him and you're saying that  he does have the power  of power be big so why doesn't the stuff  get done i mean if you look at the  polling the individual ideas from the  democratic party your party are very  popular but then you look at democrats  and often they are not popular so what's  going on here look part of it is we have  a lot of ideas and  we're out there fighting for different  pieces of this why is buildback better  so big  it's because basically the train leaves  the station only one time a year using  reconciliation where you can get a vote  of 50 you can't put things like voting  rights on it but you can put all the  economic package together but right now  the train's not leaving the station at  all and you are right on that point so  we're going to have to rearrange in  effect what goes on the train but let me  say this  offer just a little bit of sympathy for  the fact that what we're trying to do is  we're trying to fight for everybody  we're trying to fight for our babies  we're trying to fight for our seniors  we're trying to fight for people with  diabetes we're trying to fight for  people who need a government on their  side and yeah we may have tried to load  too much onto this train but by god i'd  rather have people who are trying to  fight for the american people out there  trying to do it instead of everybody  hanging back and just saying i tell what  let's cut deals in the back room and  make this thing move smoothly senator  warren thank you so much for building  our questions and thank you for the  passion  and thank you for continuing the fight
 

